### Underlying benchmark data (one layer up from PoisonedRAG)

Each record in these files pairs a PoisonedRAG-authored adversarial passage with
a benchmark question and gold answer carried over verbatim from the source QA
datasets (native ids are preserved, e.g. HotpotQA `5adbf0a2...`, MS MARCO
`1163399`). Those questions/answers are not PoisonedRAG's work; they originate
in, and should be cited to:

- Natural Questions -- Kwiatkowski et al., TACL 2019 (`nq.json`).
- HotpotQA -- Yang et al., EMNLP 2018, CC BY-SA 4.0 (`hotpotqa.json`).
- MS MARCO -- Nguyen et al., 2016 (`msmarco.json`); note MS MARCO's own
  non-commercial terms govern that data.

PoisonedRAG assembled these subsets via the BEIR benchmark (Thakur et al.,
NeurIPS 2021). Only the adversarial passages are PoisonedRAG's own contribution.

## Method / citation

The PoisonedRAG attack is reimplemented from: "PoisonedRAG: Knowledge
Corruption Attacks to Retrieval-Augmented Generation of Large Language Models,"
arXiv:2402.07867 (USENIX Security 2025). When reporting numbers produced with
this module, cite the PoisonedRAG paper.
